        "title": "Analytic Continuation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Analytic continuation is the process of extending a holomorphic function beyond its original domain of definition. The key fact making this possible: a holomorphic function is uniquely determined by its values on any set with an accumulation point (Identity Theorem). So if two definitions of a function agree on an overlapping region, they *must* agree everywhere they are both defined. This rigidity allows systematic extension."
